id: pm-graph-cif6
title: Collapse equivalent graph nodes while preserving boundary explanations
description: "Acceptance: reachability for every selected boundary pair equals the original directed graph; 1000 repeated leaves collapse with all IDs retained; cycles and unknown endpoints stay visible. Provide typed SDK and CLI, compact JSON/TOON, bounded strict input validation, typed refusals with remedies, docs and public-tracker read-only validation. Overlap audit: core SDK graph owns traversal, SCC topology, paths and relationship assembly; pm-graph export shaping removes nodes by root/depth/type/status. Sibling pm-brief context selection and pm-gantt-chart scheduling do not implement boundary-equivalent contraction. This feature is an ephemeral representation projection over existing graph data, not another algorithm store."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T22:46:57.887Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T23:09:42.752Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:47:11.966Z",codex-agent,"Design: exact stored directed-edge reachability over an explicit boundary list and selected edge types, independent of status names. SDK RelationshipGraph closure/shortestPath and analyzeKnowledgeGraph own traversal and SCC analysis. Group non-boundary acyclic known nodes by identical inbound/outbound boundary reachability signatures. Keep all cyclic and unknown nodes singleton. Membership and original witnesses remain expandable. No import, mutation, sync, journal, lease, idempotency or shared-state path is introduced; state/retry/interleaving requirements apply only if scope changes. Strict bounded schema at the pure SDK boundary; CLI reads listAllComplete without extensions. Validate against independent graph models and a public tracker copy."
  "2026-10-25T22:56:08.740Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed contractGraph and contractionInputFromGraph, CLI contract, exact boundary signatures, SCC/unknown singletons, expandable full membership, typed refusals and finite output guards. Core SDK IDs are encoded reversibly so its normalization cannot collapse exact whitespace identities. Behavioral revert proof: changing only contractGraph grouping to singleton pass-through made both selected regressions fail (2 failures: equivalent nodes failed to collapse; 1001 nodes remained instead of 2); restored the function afterward. Public committed tracker copy at origin/main 2380867: 106 items/nodes, 13 edges, 10 groups, 7 summary edges, 64 ordered boundary pairs checked, 90.566 percent node reduction, 42457 original JSON bytes vs 11180 contracted bytes, 0 cycles/unknowns in this source; input item/settings/history hashes unchanged. Synthetic tests cover cycles and missing endpoints separately. No import/sync/mutation path is added; seeded SDK read-back and replay tests validate the read-only surface."
  "2026-10-25T22:57:33.827Z",codex-agent,"Targeted verification passed 19/19 (no skipped/canceled tests), including real pinned-host JSON/TOON with no git executable, 500 graph sequences/6000 transitions, 500 read-only SDK state export/replay sequences, and generated custom active/blocked/terminal_done/terminal_canceled registry names. Typecheck, canonical lint, zero-duplication and docstring gates passed at unchanged policies. New tests seed native metadata, parent/blocker/dependency relationships, bodies and CRLF values; all native fields are compared through SDK complete-list read-back against the reference snapshot. Full npm/Bun release gates are reserved for CI on the saturated host."
  "2026-10-25T22:59:28.555Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/pull/166 . Implementation commit 16ce4c7. Initial CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-graph/actions/runs/40242645091 is running; exact final-head npm/Bun release counts and run URL will be recorded in the PR before handoff. Strict local pm health passed with zero findings after restoring the CI-pinned project extension. Known limits: row budgets are not token budgets; group IDs require an unchanged snapshot; summary loops do not assert original cycles; no tracker import or existing Neo4j sync attestation is claimed. Releasing the claim for orchestrator review while leaving this item in progress as required; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-25T23:08:25.862Z",codex-agent,"CI found a release-gate evidence gap: final-head Node 22 passed 407/407, Windows passed 1+4, and Node 26 tests passed, but the Bun-driven release gate measured 99.6345 percent overall line coverage below the unchanged 99.7 threshold. New contraction source coverage is 100 percent lines; the uncovered new validator pagination loop combines with runtime-specific legacy uncovered paths. Adding a real non-git tracker fixture with enough SDK relationships to force multiple validation pages, then rerunning targeted tests and CI. No threshold changes."
  "2026-10-25T23:09:42.168Z",codex-agent,"Closed the CI evidence gap with a real non-git 34-node associative tracker (>1000 summary edges), forcing validator pagination and checking all 64 boundary pairs plus unchanged source bytes. Targeted validator coverage command: node --test --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=scripts/validate-contraction.ts test/contraction-command.test.ts ; passed 5/5 with validator 100 percent lines/functions. The linked pm test run passed 19/19 again; typecheck, lint and zero-duplication passed. Final-head release gates and exact counts will be recorded in PR 166 after CI; no thresholds changed. Claim released for the required review handoff; item remains open."
